{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3a33af34e4d8a7902accddd8202823e2b0ce620ff5465512410b87271857e67b","digest":{"component_or_area":"mapping seam configuration and documentation","key_entities":["[tool.rebar.mapping]","docs/config.md","docs/mapping-seam.md","docs/README.md","CHANGELOG",".bridge_state/projects.json","probe command","status","type","link","priority","create_defaults"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","portability","mapping seam","provider-neutral","migration safety","configuration","reuse contract"],"propositions":["The mapping seam configuration surface requires end-to-end documentation covering axis catalog, merge layers, per-project keying, and fail-closed validation.","The mapping seam must work across diverse CI environments and offline; no capability's only trigger can be a specific provider to satisfy the portability criterion.","The feature is additive and backward-compatible: absent [tool.rebar.mapping] section reproduces current hardcoded behavior; rollback is deletion of the section.","The provider-neutral core of the mapping seam establishes the reuse contract for future integrations (Linear, GitLab, GitHub-Issues) whose direct support is out of scope.","All mapping seam behaviors are covered by unit tests with injected transports requiring no live Jira and no specific CI provider."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787705318589949001,"uuid":"35793e9d-100e-4adb-a962-c9d87c6c2605"}